{
 "_readme": [
  "Hubs for the OpenStreetMap second-hand pull (mapsee_ingest_osm_secondhand.py).",
  "Same shape as osm_food_sources.json: centre + radius_miles, one entry per",
  "metro, tiled by the ingest.",
  "",
  "TILES ARE 1.2 DEGREES HERE, NOT osm-food's 0.35 - see TILE_DEG in the ingest.",
  "This selector is an order of magnitude sparser than restaurants, so inheriting",
  "the food tile size cut every hub into ~35 near-empty cells. Measured on the",
  "first production sweep (run 32335784569): ~9s per tile, ~5 minutes per hub,",
  "and thirteen hubs ran the warm step past its 45-minute cap. At 1.2 a hub is",
  "~4 cells, so 32 hubs cost ~148 tiles where 13 used to cost ~455.",
  "",
  "ORDERED BY MEASURED DENSITY, not by size of city. Second-hand supply skews",
  "UK/EU hard and the US is the weak market - the reverse of every other lens -",
  "so the US hubs are last. Measured 2026-08-19, city-tagged venues with readable",
  "hours (shop=second_hand + shop=charity only):",
  "",
  "  London 150   Berlin 56   Helsinki 40   Edinburgh 35   Wien 29",
  "  's-Gravenhage 29   Cambridge 28   Norwich 28   Bristol 25   Budapest 25",
  "",
  "Those are a FLOOR: addr:city is present on only 35-39% of the pool, which",
  "limits the counting instrument and not the data. The live sweep bore that out",
  "- Edinburgh was forecast at 35 and returned 167 rows at a 50-mile radius.",
  "",
  "A 50-mile radius is deliberate for this category. Charity shops are a HIGH",
  "STREET institution, so the interesting density is in the towns around a city",
  "rather than its centre: the London hub swallows most of the south-east, and",
  "Leeds covers Sheffield, Bradford and York.",
  "",
  "Adding a hub is cheap - this adapter fetches nobody's website, so a hub costs",
  "a handful of Overpass tiles once a month and nothing else. What it is NOT free",
  "of: a city only gets a crawlable /c/<slug> landing page if it is also in",
  "../mapsee/src/cities.js. Edinburgh, Helsinki and Vienna were all synced and",
  "invisible to search for exactly that reason."
 ],
